---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How much should Shopify SEO cost for a small skincare brand in India?",
    answer: "Realistic monthly retainers for a small-to-mid D2C skincare store run roughly ₹20,000–₹75,000, based on 2026 India SEO pricing data — below that range, most agencies can't cover technical audits, YMYL-grade content, and link building simultaneously.",
  },
  {
    question: "How long does Shopify SEO take to show results?",
    answer: "Most 2026 India-market guides put initial movement at 3–6 months, with stronger compounding results at 6–12 months, which is consistent with SEO timelines across categories, not specific to skincare.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is SEO better than paid ads for a new D2C skincare brand?",
    answer: "They serve different jobs — SEO compounds over time and lowers long-term cost per acquisition, while ads give you immediate visibility while the SEO foundation is being built. Most brands need both running in parallel, not one instead of the other.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Best SEO Agency for Shopify Skincare Stores: A Founder's Checklist",
  "description": "What separates a good Shopify SEO agency from a generic one — a practical checklist for D2C skincare founders, with real pricing benchmarks and red flags to avoid.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Unitscalers",
    "url": "https://unitscalers.com"
  },
  "url": "https://unitscalers.com/blog/best-seo-agency-shopify-skincare",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26",
  "articleSection": "SEO"
};
---

<Layout
  title="Best SEO Agency for Shopify Skincare Stores: A Founder's Checklist | Unitscalers"
  description="What separates a good Shopify SEO agency from a generic one — a practical checklist for D2C skincare founders, with real pricing benchmarks and red flags to avoid."
  schema={schema}
>
  <!-- Article Header -->
  <article>
    <header class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-12 py-16 md:py-24">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600 mb-8">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-dark dark:hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-brand-dark dark:hover:text-white transition-colors">Blog</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <span class="text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-700 truncate">Article 01</span>
        </nav>

        <!-- Tags -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest bg-brand-dark text-brand-green px-3 py-1">Shopify SEO</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600">Comparison · Founder Checklist</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600">6 min read</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-brand-dark dark:text-white mb-6">
          Best SEO Agency for Shopify Skincare Stores: A Founder's Checklist
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
          Choosing an SEO agency for a Shopify skincare store comes down to three questions: does the agency understand Shopify's platform-specific technical issues, does it understand the stricter content standard Google applies to skincare, and does its pricing match the scope it's promising. Most agencies fail at least one of these.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Article Body -->
    <div class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-12">
        <div class="prose-like text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">

          <!-- Section 1 -->
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-dark dark:text-white mt-0 mb-6">
            Why generic SEO advice doesn't work for Shopify skincare stores
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
            A general-purpose SEO agency treats every ecommerce client the same way: keyword research, some blog posts, a handful of backlinks. That approach misses two things that are specific to this exact combination of platform and category.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
            First, Shopify generates SEO problems automatically, out of the box, regardless of what the merchant does. Collection pages, filter combinations, tag pages, and pagination all create duplicate URLs the moment a store is set up — this isn't a mistake a brand made, it's how the platform works by default. An agency that hasn't specifically audited Shopify stores before will often miss this entirely, because it's invisible until rankings quietly decline.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-12">
            Second, skincare sits in Google's "Your Money or Your Life" (YMYL) category whenever a product page or blog post talks about actives — glycolic acid, retinol, salicylic acid — or makes any claim that could affect a reader's skin health. Google's Search Quality Evaluator Guidelines hold YMYL content to a measurably higher bar than a general retail page, and a 2024 Google Search Central update specifically flagged anonymous authorship and thin product descriptions as stronger negative signals in health and wellness categories than in other retail verticals.
          </p>

          <!-- Section 2 — Checklist -->
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-dark dark:text-white mb-8">
            The checklist
          </h2>

          <!-- Checklist Items -->
          <div class="space-y-6 mb-12">
            {[
              {
                num: "01",
                title: "Ask for a Shopify-specific technical audit before any content work starts",
                body: "A credible agency should be able to name your store's duplicate-URL sources (collection/tag paths, filter parameters, pagination) without you telling them where to look. If the first thing they propose is blog content, that's a sequencing problem — fixing platform-level technical issues has to come before content investment, or the content is built on a leaking foundation.",
              },
              {
                num: "02",
                title: "Ask how they handle YMYL/E-E-A-T for skincare content specifically",
                body: "Do they attach real author bios and credentials to product-adjacent content? Do they have a review process for ingredient claims? If the answer is vague, the content they produce is unlikely to hold up under Google's stricter evaluation for health-adjacent categories.",
              },
              {
                num: "03",
                title: "Compare pricing against realistic 2026 India benchmarks",
                body: "Freelancers in India typically charge somewhere between ₹8,000 and ₹40,000 a month; agencies range roughly ₹20,000 to over ₹2,00,000 depending on scope (Socio Labs, 6ix Marketers, BeTopSEO, 2026). A ₹5,000/month \"full SEO\" package and a ₹1,50,000/month package can both use the same words to describe very different scopes of work — the deliverable list matters more than the sticker price.",
              },
              {
                num: "04",
                title: "Ask what they exclude, not just what they include",
                body: "A trustworthy agency will tell you upfront what fabricated proof looks like and refuse to use it — no invented case studies, no purchased reviews, no AggregateRating schema without real reviews behind it. Google's own guidance treats fabricated review schema as a common cause of manual penalties.",
              },
              {
                num: "05",
                title: "Check whether they specialize or generalize",
                body: "Specialization isn't just a branding choice — it changes delivery quality. Niche specialists achieve roughly 78% client retention vs. 54% for generalists (Agency Acquisitions Insights, 2026). For a problem as technically narrow as Shopify SEO for a YMYL category, repetition in the exact intersection matters more than general marketing competence.",
              },
            ].map((item) => (
              <div class="border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-black p-6 md:p-8 flex gap-5">
                <div class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-gray-100 dark:text-gray-800 select-none flex-shrink-0 leading-none mt-1">
                  {item.num}
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="font-bold text-brand-dark dark:text-white mb-3 text-base md:text-lg">{item.title}</h3>
                  <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <!-- Pricing table -->
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-dark dark:text-white mb-6">
            2026 India SEO pricing benchmarks at a glance
          </h2>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="bg-brand-dark dark:bg-gray-800 text-white">
                  <th class="text-left font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest py-3 px-4 border border-gray-700">Option</th>
                  <th class="text-left font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest py-3 px-4 border border-gray-700">Typical Monthly Cost (India)</th>
                  <th class="text-left font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest py-3 px-4 border border-gray-700">Best Fit</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {[
                  { option: "Freelancer", cost: "₹8,000 – ₹40,000", fit: "Narrow, well-defined scope; tight budget" },
                  { option: "Specialist agency", cost: "₹20,000 – ₹2,00,000+", fit: "Technical + content + link-building together" },
                  { option: "In-house hire", cost: "₹40,000 – ₹1,50,000+ salary", fit: "Later-stage brands with sustained scope" },
                ].map((row, i) => (
                  <tr class={`border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 ${i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white dark:bg-black' : 'bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900'}`}>
                    <td class="py-3 px-4 border-r border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 font-medium text-brand-dark dark:text-white">{row.option}</td>
                    <td class="py-3 px-4 border-r border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 font-mono text-xs text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">{row.cost}</td>
                    <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">{row.fit}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600 mt-2 font-mono">Source: Socio Labs, 6ix Marketers, BeTopSEO, Vansh Bohra — 2026 India SEO pricing surveys</p>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ section -->
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-dark dark:text-white mb-8">FAQ</h2>
          <div class="space-y-4 mb-12">
            {faqs.map((faq) => (
              <div class="border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-black">
                <details class="group">
                  <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-5 md:p-6 font-bold text-brand-dark dark:text-white text-sm md:text-base list-none">
                    <span>{faq.question}</span>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform flex-shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                      <path d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
                    </svg>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="px-5 md:px-6 pb-5 md:pb-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 pt-4">
                    {faq.answer}
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <!-- Source note -->
          <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-black">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600 mb-2">Sources</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              SEO pricing India 2026: Socio Labs, 6ix Marketers, Vansh Bohra, BeTopSEO, Ranking Partner, Digital Dot Agency.
              YMYL/E-E-A-T for wellness ecommerce: 1Digital Agency (2026), Tygart Media (2026), The Stacc (2026).
              All statistics are from third-party industry research, not Unitscalers' own client results.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Related articles -->
        <div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600 mb-6">Continue reading</div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <a href="/blog/hidden-shopify-seo-problems-skincare" class="group border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-black p-5 hover:border-brand-dark dark:hover:border-gray-400 transition-all">
              <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-green mb-2">Article 02</div>
              <div class="font-bold text-brand-dark dark:text-white text-sm group-hover:underline underline-offset-2 leading-snug">The Hidden Shopify SEO Problems Costing Skincare Brands Rankings →</div>
            </a>
            <a href="/blog" class="group border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-black p-5 hover:border-brand-dark dark:hover:border-gray-400 transition-all flex items-center">
              <div>
                <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-600 mb-2">All Articles</div>
                <div class="font-bold text-brand-dark dark:text-white text-sm group-hover:underline underline-offset-2">View the full blog →</div>
              </div>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="py-16 bg-brand-dark dark:bg-gray-900 text-white border-t border-gray-800">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">Want a Shopify SEO audit for your skincare store?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8 leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base">
          We audit your store's technical architecture, duplicate-URL issues, and ranking signals before touching a single piece of content.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact-us" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest bg-white text-brand-dark px-8 py-4 hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
          Book a Free Audit
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
